<body>

  <h1>BITS Pilani Digital</h1>
  <h2>CodeForge V1.0 • Official Bug Fix Log & Diagnostic Audit</h2>

  <div class="meta-box">
    <p style="margin:0 0 4pt 0;"><strong>Candidate:</strong> Aditya Jaiswal</p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 4pt 0;"><strong>GitHub Repository:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/ajaditya103-a11y/BitsAssignmentcodeforge">ajaditya103-a11y/BitsAssignmentcodeforge</a></p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 4pt 0;"><strong>Live Application:</strong> <a href="https://bitsgrade.netlify.app/">https://bitsgrade.netlify.app</a></p>
    <p style="margin:0;"><strong>Date:</strong> September 27, 2026</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Executive Summary</h3>
  <p>
    This document serves as the formal <strong>Stage 1 (Debug)</strong> submission deliverable for the BITS Digital CodeForge V1.0 challenge.
    All 12 identified bugs spanning data ingestion, boundary mathematical continuity, statistical calculation, canvas coordinate projection, 
    and output serialization have been completely diagnosed, rooted, fixed, and verified across automated and manual test scenarios.
  </p>

  <h3>Master Bug Fix Log (Official Table)</h3>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 5%;">#</th>
        <th style="width: 23%;">Bug / Issue Identified</th>
        <th style="width: 22%;">How You Reproduced It</th>
        <th style="width: 25%;">Root Cause</th>
        <th style="width: 25%;">Fix Implemented & Tested</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">1</td>
        <td><strong>Inverted Min and Max Stat Cards</strong></td>
        <td>Uploaded sample marks; the Min card displayed the highest score (e.g. 98) while the Max card displayed the lowest score (e.g. 12).</td>
        <td>HTML markup IDs were swapped: <code>&lt;b id="max"&gt;</code> was placed in the Min card, and <code>&lt;b id="min"&gt;</code> in the Max card.</td>
        <td>Swapped IDs to <code>#minStat</code> and <code>#maxStat</code> to align with card labels. Verified across 3 datasets: Min displays lowest and Max displays highest.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">2</td>
        <td><strong>Course List Duplication & Stale Dropdown Options</strong></td>
        <td>Uploaded a file containing 50 records of "CS F111", or uploaded a second file sequentially without refreshing.</td>
        <td><code>file.onchange</code> mapped directly over student rows without deduplication, and <code>course.innerHTML</code> was never cleared on re-upload.</td>
        <td>Reset <code>course.innerHTML</code> on upload, extracted distinct names using <code>Array.from(new Set(...))</code>. Tested with 100+ row multi-course file.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">3</td>
        <td><strong>File Picker Rejection of Modern .xlsx Files</strong></td>
        <td>Attempted to select standard modern <code>.xlsx</code> spreadsheet in operating system file dialog.</td>
        <td>The file input element had <code>accept=".xls"</code>, preventing or hiding standard <code>.xlsx</code> spreadsheets.</td>
        <td>Updated attribute to <code>accept=".xlsx, .xls, .csv"</code>. Tested picking and dragging <code>.xlsx</code>, <code>.xls</code>, and <code>.csv</code> workbooks.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">4</td>
        <td><strong>Division by Zero (NaN) on Empty or Uniform Datasets</strong></td>
        <td>Selected an empty course, or a cohort where all students scored identical marks (e.g., all 75).</td>
        <td><code>computeStats()</code> divided by <code>m.length</code> without checking for zero. Uniform marks yielded &sigma; = 0, causing division by zero in Gaussian PDF.</td>
        <td>Added early empty-dataset guards returning "—", and clamped &sigma; = max(&sigma;, 0.5). Tested with 0 students and 50 uniform students without errors.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">5</td>
        <td><strong>Bell Curve X-Axis Misaligned with Histogram Bins</strong></td>
        <td>Inspected canvas overlay. The Gaussian curve peak drifted progressively leftward as marks increased towards 100.</td>
        <td>Histogram bars used step size of 32px (30 + i &times; 32), while bell curve used 30px (30 + (x/10) &times; 30). Different coordinate spaces.</td>
        <td>Unified coordinate system with shared step size (34px) and bar width. Tested normal distributions; peak aligns exactly with cohort mean (&mu;).</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">6</td>
        <td><strong>Concurrent Animation Frame Leak on Rapid Changes</strong></td>
        <td>Quickly adjusted grade boundary dropdowns or switched courses repeatedly.</td>
        <td><code>drawHistogram()</code> launched new <code>requestAnimationFrame(animate)</code> loops on every change without cancelling active loops.</td>
        <td>Tracked <code>currentAnimFrameId</code> and invoked <code>cancelAnimationFrame()</code> before spawning any new animation loop. Rapid scrubbing observed at stable 60 FPS.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">7</td>
        <td><strong>Fractional Marks Fall Through Boundaries (Grade Loss)</strong></td>
        <td>Inputted non-integer marks such as 79.4 or 69.8. Student received no grade and was excluded from CSV export.</td>
        <td>Boundaries are discrete integers (70-79 then 80-100). A mark of 79.4 is &gt; 79 and &lt; 80, so it matched neither condition.</td>
        <td>Added mandatory integer rounding (<code>Math.round(Number(marks))</code>) during ingestion per BITS policy (80.2 &rarr; 81, 79.4 &rarr; 79). Verified 100% grade assignment.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">8</td>
        <td><strong>Premature Timer Start & Permanent Post-Export Freeze</strong></td>
        <td>Opened page, waited 10 minutes before picking a file; timer counted idle time. Clicking download stopped timer permanently.</td>
        <td><code>gradingStartTime</code> was captured at page evaluation. <code>download.onclick</code> invoked <code>clearInterval()</code> with no resume mechanism.</td>
        <td>Tied timer initiation to active course selection. Added pause/resume tracking and immediate first-second tick display. Verified timer accuracy.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">9</td>
        <td><strong>Grade Cascade Allows Negative Values & Invalid Selects</strong></td>
        <td>Decreased Grade A Min down towards 0. Lower dropdowns set to -1, causing unselected or corrupted select states.</td>
        <td><code>cascadeMaxFrom()</code> set <code>targetMax = prevMin - 1</code>. When <code>prevMin = 0</code>, target was -1, which does not exist in options (0..100).</td>
        <td>Clamped target values using <code>Math.max(0, prevMin - 1)</code> and enforced Min &lt; Max. Tested lowering boundaries to 0; clamped cleanly.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">10</td>
        <td><strong>CSV Export Lacks Boundary Validation & Field Escaping</strong></td>
        <td>Exported CSV when instructor name had a comma (e.g. "Sharma, Dr. P.") or when marks fell outside unvalidated ranges.</td>
        <td>Raw string concatenation without RFC 4180 quotes. Students outside ranges produced empty or missing grade records silently.</td>
        <td>Implemented RFC 4180 compliant CSV quoting function, validated 100% student grade matching, and cleaned memory via <code>URL.revokeObjectURL()</code>.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">11</td>
        <td><strong>CSS Animation Class Removed Before Transition Renders</strong></td>
        <td>Observed card lift effect when changing select option; cards snapped instantly with visual stutter.</td>
        <td><code>setTimeout(() =&gt; card.classList.remove("lift"), 30)</code> removed class after 30ms, while CSS transition was set to 250ms.</td>
        <td>Adjusted timeout to 250ms matching the CSS transition duration. Tested select changes; verified smooth, fluid card elevation.</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold;">12</td>
        <td><strong>Full Scale Coverage [0–100] Boundary Check Missing</strong></td>
        <td>Set Grade A Max to 90 or Grade E Min to 10; validation passed despite scores 91-100 and 0-9 having no assigned grade.</td>
        <td><code>validateRanges()</code> only evaluated internal adjacent boundaries, omitting checks for global scale endpoints (0 and 100).</td>
        <td>Enforced strict endpoint validation (<code>Amax === 100</code> and <code>Emin === 0</code>). Tested setting A Max to 95; UI flagged error and blocked export.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Stage 2 Reimagined Enhancements Summary</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>One-Click Academic Grading Presets:</strong> BITS Default, Statistical Bell Curve (&mu; &plusmn; &sigma;), Lenient, and Strict profiles.</li>
    <li><strong>Live Student Grade Audit Roster:</strong> Real-time student table with instant search and automatic Borderline (&plusmn;1 mark) warnings.</li>
    <li><strong>Continuous Grade Spectrum Visualizer:</strong> Dynamic 0–100 multi-segmented color spectrum confirming 100% continuous coverage.</li>
    <li><strong>Advanced Academic Statistics:</strong> Adds Standard Deviation (&sigma;), Interquartile Range (IQR), and Class Passing Rate %.</li>
    <li><strong>In-App Demo Dataset & Template Generator:</strong> One-click simulation with 144 students across 3 courses and downloadable blank .xlsx templates.</li>
    <li><strong>Dual-Format Export Suite:</strong> Clean RFC 4180 CSV export and formatted multi-sheet Excel (.xlsx) workbooks with executive summary.</li>
  </ol>

  <p style="margin-top:24pt; border-top:1pt solid #cbd5e1; padding-top:8pt; font-size:9pt; color:#64748b; text-align:center;">
    BITS Pilani Digital • Advanced Academic Grading Console • CodeForge Challenge V1.0 • Candidate: Aditya Jaiswal
  </p>

</body>
</html>
